[engl]
{100}{}{Razlo}
{200}{}{Doctor for Shady Sands.}
{1000}{}{Predialogue installations}
{1010}{}{First dialogue}
{1020}{}{Second time}
{1030}{}{Player is in bad shape}
{1040}{}{Its night}
{2000}{}{I'm Razlo. Can I help you?}
{2010}{}{Not right now, but it was nice meeting you.}
{2020}{}{I need healing.}
{2030}{}{I am quite interested into medicine myself, and this is the reason I am visiting you today. My hopes are that you could share some of your knowledge and experience with me...}
{3000}{}{You look distraught. Are you in need of assistance?}
{3010}{}{I need healing.}
{3020}{}{Nevermind.}
{4000}{}{Hello, again. How can I be of service?}
{4010}{}{Hello again. Just stopping by.}
{4020}{}{What do you know about Radscorpions?}
{4030}{}{I have a sample of the Radscorpion poison, can you do
something with it?}
{5000}{}{I think I can cure what ails ya. It's gonna cost you @lex price@$ bucks.}
{5010}{}{Well... all right. That sounds fair.}
{5020}{}{Changed my mind. I'll be back later.}
{6000}{}{That should do it. Good luck, youngster.}
{6010}{}{[End.]}
{7000}{}{Sure, sure... We can already arrange something, I guess. But I would like to have something in return, a kind of compensation for my time and work. It's not that I'm trying to earn something out of this, but a help from a colleague like you would be quite appreciated. I'll keep it short then -- I would need $1500 for a short lesson or $3000 for one with more detail. Please, let me know when you have it.}
{7010}{}{You don't have to worry, my appreciated colleague, I have $1500 right here! [You give him $1500]}
{7020}{}{Well, I should start gathering some healing herbs then. See you later, doctor!}
{8000}{}{It was nice seeing you again. Have a good day.}
{8010}{}{[End.]}
{9000}{}{It's late. Come back in the morning.}
{9010}{}{But I need your help.}
{9020}{}{Hnn.}
{10000}{}{Hnn?! What is that? Great, I get awakened by the great mumbling beast of the north. Come back in the morning.}
{10010}{}{[End.]}
{11000}{}{Sure, about what?}
{11010}{}{What do you know about Radscorpions?}
{11020}{}{Nothing at all.}
{12000}{}{Not too much. They seem to be extremely large versions
of the north American Emperor scorpion. Contrary to my
medical knowledge, their poison has grown more potent,
not diluted, as I would expect. Seth has been hunting them,
which helps some of my tests.}
{12010}{}{[More...]}
{12020}{}{You seem well educated. What are you doing here?}
{13000}{}{And how such a large creature can even be possible by natural evolution, or even radiation induced mutation is beyond me.}
{13010}{}{I need something for their poison.}
{13020}{}{Thanks}
{13030}{}{[More..]}
{14000}{}{Doc Morbid in Junktown taught me some. And just because we live in stone huts, does not mean we are less intelligent or educated. Have a nice day.}
{14010}{}{[Exit.]}
{15000}{}{If I had a sample of their poison, I could create a cure.}
{15010}{}{I will find a sample.}
{16000}{}{Here, let's see.}
{16010}{}{[Next...]}
{17000}{}{Yep, just as I thought. Let me get the cure.}
{17010}{}{[Next...]}
{18000}{}{You seem fine, now. Be careful in the future.}
{18010}{}{[End.]}
{19000}{}{They seem to be sensitive to light. Nocturnal. If I
could get a sample of their poison, especially the
venom production sac located in their tail, I could
create an anti-venom.}
{19010}{}{[End.]}
{20000}{}{Here, take this as a free sample. It seems to work
well against radscorpion stings, of course, but it
shows much potential as a general anti-venom and
poison cure.}
{20010}{}{Thank you.}

